From: Muhammad Huda Nugroho <mhudan21@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: dwmac-ipq5018: advertise only 2500BASEX on PCS GMAC1

GMAC1 on the IPQ5018 drives an external 2.5G PHY (the RTL8221B on the
QDM530 lan2 port) through the UNIPHY PCS. The driver advertises SGMII,
1000BASEX and 2500BASEX for that port. Because the RTL8221B is a
Clause-45 PHY, offering SGMII alongside 2500BASEX makes it select the
2500BASEX/SGMII auto-switch SerDes mode (rate_matching = NONE): for a 1G
copper peer the PHY drops its SerDes to SGMII and expects the UNIPHY to
be reconfigured to SGMII at runtime. That runtime switch is unreliable
on this hardware - the 1G link comes up but data does not flow reliably.

Advertise only 2500BASEX for the PCS-backed GMAC1 so the RTL8221B stays
in the fixed 2500BASEX rate-matching mode (rate_matching = PAUSE): its
SerDes is pinned at 2500BASEX and it pause-rate-adapts 1G/100/10 copper
speeds internally, leaving the UNIPHY permanently at 2500BASEX. GMAC0
(no PCS, internal GE PHY) keeps plain SGMII.

Signed-off-by: Muhammad Huda Nugroho <mhudan21@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-ipq5018.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-ipq5018.c
@@ -112,13 +112,18 @@
 
 	/*
 	 * IPQ5018 has two GMACs:
-	 * - GMAC0 supports SGMII and is wired to the SoC's internal GE PHY
-	 * - GMAC1 supports SGMII, 1000BaseX, and 2500BaseX, configurable by
-	 *   the UNIPHY PCS
+	 * - GMAC0 is wired to the SoC's internal GE PHY over SGMII (no PCS).
+	 * - GMAC1 drives an external 2.5G PHY through the UNIPHY PCS.
+	 *
+	 * For GMAC1 advertise only 2500BASEX (not SGMII/1000BASEX) so a
+	 * rate-matching capable PHY (e.g. the RTL8221B) keeps its SerDes
+	 * fixed at 2500BASEX and pause-rate-adapts slower copper speeds
+	 * internally. Advertising SGMII as well makes such PHYs pick the
+	 * 2500BASEX/SGMII auto-switch mode, which needs the UNIPHY switched
+	 * to SGMII at runtime for 1G links; that switch is unreliable here
+	 * and leaves 1G peers linked but without stable data flow.
 	 */
-	__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII, interfaces);
 	if (priv->hw->phylink_pcs) {
-		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_1000BASEX, interfaces);
 		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX, interfaces);
 
 		/*
